"For each item below, fetch its source and check that the recorded quote appears on the page and supports the item. A card item is a field of the plan in the producer's words, with the sources it cites: check each factual claim in it against those sources, and any value it carries against the page; what the plan will build, measure or predict needs no source, but a factual claim with no source is UNSUPPORTED. For a cost input, check that the page states the number for the setting given; whether it applies to this plan is not yours to judge. When the page states a different number for a num or rate item, give it as page_value. Decide only from the pages you fetch and the text below; do not read files. Return one status per item, under its ref: SUPPORTED, PARTIAL, UNSUPPORTED, CONTRADICTED or UNREACHABLE, with the page sentence you relied on.
Items, one per line:
{\"ref\":\"card:question\",\"text\":\"Will graphics-card molecular simulations using Green–Kubo on C10–C50 hydrocarbons and esters rank immersion coolants' viscosity and thermal conductivity the same way measurements do?\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:hypothesis\",\"text\":\"Green–Kubo MD with one fixed force field has a chemistry-dependent error floor near 25 percent that more molecules cannot remove [s_ogbomo_res].\",\"sources\":[{\"id\":\"s_ogbomo_res\",\"url\":\"https://spiral.imperial.ac.uk/server/api/core/bitstreams/fa07c113-8958-4f1e-a010-0ef2bfc39e17/content\",\"quote\":\"Density is reproduced to within 4% for seven of the eight molecules at 40 °C. Viscosity errors are small for the pure hydrocarbons with LOPLS, but this property is consistently under-predicted for the oxygen-containing molecules; the reference ranking of the fluids is nonetheless largely preserved. Thermal conductivity is over-predicted for every molecule, by amounts that correlate with the density of aliphatic C–H bonds, compressing the reference range and misordering the fluids.\"}]}
{\"ref\":\"card:if_lever\",\"text\":\"At 120 molecules, held-out viscosity error after bias correction falls below 15 percent and rank correlation with measurement exceeds 0.9 [s_ogbomo_res].\",\"sources\":[{\"id\":\"s_ogbomo_res\",\"url\":\"https://spiral.imperial.ac.uk/server/api/core/bitstreams/fa07c113-8958-4f1e-a010-0ef2bfc39e17/content\",\"quote\":\"Density is reproduced to within 4% for seven of the eight molecules at 40 °C. Viscosity errors are small for the pure hydrocarbons with LOPLS, but this property is consistently under-predicted for the oxygen-containing molecules; the reference ranking of the fluids is nonetheless largely preserved. Thermal conductivity is over-predicted for every molecule, by amounts that correlate with the density of aliphatic C–H bonds, compressing the reference range and misordering the fluids.\"}]}
{\"ref\":\"card:if_not\",\"text\":\"Held-out viscosity error stays above 25 percent and rank correlation below 0.7 at every set size, capping candidate ranking [s_ogbomo_res].\",\"sources\":[{\"id\":\"s_ogbomo_res\",\"url\":\"https://spiral.imperial.ac.uk/server/api/core/bitstreams/fa07c113-8958-4f1e-a010-0ef2bfc39e17/content\",\"quote\":\"Density is reproduced to within 4% for seven of the eight molecules at 40 °C. Viscosity errors are small for the pure hydrocarbons with LOPLS, but this property is consistently under-predicted for the oxygen-containing molecules; the reference ranking of the fluids is nonetheless largely preserved. Thermal conductivity is over-predicted for every molecule, by amounts that correlate with the density of aliphatic C–H bonds, compressing the reference range and misordering the fluids.\"}]}
{\"ref\":\"card:test_summary\",\"text\":\"One LAMMPS LOPLS-AA Green–Kubo protocol at 40 °C, six five-nanosecond replicas per molecule, run on 8, 24, 48 then 120 molecules from the public 835-molecule reference set, scored only against measured viscosity and thermal conductivity [s_ogbomo_db].\",\"sources\":[{\"id\":\"s_ogbomo_db\",\"url\":\"https://spiral.imperial.ac.uk/entities/publication/9423c271-1953-481c-8e8d-88eeb67e2535\",\"quote\":\"We compile a database of approximately 4,700 critically evaluated reference values for the density, viscosity, and thermal conductivity of 835 unique organic molecules in the C10–C50 range.\"}]}
{\"ref\":\"card:closest_prior\",\"text\":\"Ogbomo and colleagues, in 2026, used Green–Kubo molecular dynamics to compute viscosity and thermal conductivity for eight C10–C50 molecules at 40 °C and compared with measurements [s_ogbomo_md].\",\"sources\":[{\"id\":\"s_ogbomo_md\",\"url\":\"https://spiral.imperial.ac.uk/entities/publication/9423c271-1953-481c-8e8d-88eeb67e2535\",\"quote\":\"Equilibrium molecular dynamics (EMD) simulations of eight representative molecules reproduce density accurately but show systematic, chemistry-dependent force-field errors for the viscosity and thermal conductivity.\"}],\"value\":8}
{\"ref\":\"card:left_open\",\"text\":\"Whether the error is a correctable bias or a random floor that caps ranking, and how rank agreement holds over hundreds of molecules [s_ogbomo_db].\",\"sources\":[{\"id\":\"s_ogbomo_db\",\"url\":\"https://spiral.imperial.ac.uk/entities/publication/9423c271-1953-481c-8e8d-88eeb67e2535\",\"quote\":\"We compile a database of approximately 4,700 critically evaluated reference values for the density, viscosity, and thermal conductivity of 835 unique organic molecules in the C10–C50 range.\"}]}
{\"ref\":\"card:anchor\",\"text\":\"Repeat the published eight-molecule Green–Kubo run first: density within 4% for seven molecules and thermal conductivity over-predicted for all eight [s_ogbomo_res].\",\"sources\":[{\"id\":\"s_ogbomo_res\",\"url\":\"https://spiral.imperial.ac.uk/server/api/core/bitstreams/fa07c113-8958-4f1e-a010-0ef2bfc39e17/content\",\"quote\":\"Density is reproduced to within 4% for seven of the eight molecules at 40 °C. Viscosity errors are small for the pure hydrocarbons with LOPLS, but this property is consistently under-predicted for the oxygen-containing molecules; the reference ranking of the fluids is nonetheless largely preserved. Thermal conductivity is over-predicted for every molecule, by amounts that correlate with the density of aliphatic C–H bonds, compressing the reference range and misordering the fluids.\"}],\"value\":\"density error 4% or less on 7 of 8 molecules at 40 °C\"}
{\"ref\":\"card:limits\",\"text\":\"Shows transport-property error only at 40 °C for pure liquids between 1 and 50 mPa·s, not blends or sold coolants. Cannot show ranking behaviour beyond 120 molecules.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"src:s_ogbomo_res\",\"url\":\"https://spiral.imperial.ac.uk/server/api/core/bitstreams/fa07c113-8958-4f1e-a010-0ef2bfc39e17/content\",\"quote\":\"Density is reproduced to within 4% for seven of the eight molecules at 40 °C. Viscosity errors are small for the pure hydrocarbons with LOPLS, but this property is consistently under-predicted for the oxygen-containing molecules; the reference ranking of the fluids is nonetheless largely preserved. Thermal conductivity is over-predicted for every molecule, by amounts that correlate with the density of aliphatic C–H bonds, compressing the reference range and misordering the fluids.\",\"supports\":\"anchor tolerances, the predicted error floor and the if_not expectation\"}
{\"ref\":\"src:s_ogbomo_db\",\"url\":\"https://spiral.imperial.ac.uk/entities/publication/9423c271-1953-481c-8e8d-88eeb67e2535\",\"quote\":\"We compile a database of approximately 4,700 critically evaluated reference values for the density, viscosity, and thermal conductivity of 835 unique organic molecules in the C10–C50 range.\",\"supports\":\"the measured reference set used for scoring, its size and chemical range\"}
{\"ref\":\"src:s_ogbomo_md\",\"url\":\"https://spiral.imperial.ac.uk/entities/publication/9423c271-1953-481c-8e8d-88eeb67e2535\",\"quote\":\"Equilibrium molecular dynamics (EMD) simulations of eight representative molecules reproduce density accurately but show systematic, chemistry-dependent force-field errors for the viscosity and thermal conductivity.\",\"supports\":\"the closest prior work and the baseline arm of eight molecules\"}
